      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\n- **Dose:** 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. The usual maximum for adults is 3,200 mg/day under prescriber supervision, and 1,200 mg/day for OTC use.\n- **Single dose:** 1600 mg is double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg.\n- **Risks at this level:** Doses this high raise the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. Normal kidney and liver function and no allergies don't change that.\n\nWhich of these did you intend?\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the usual maximum for anti-inflammatory dosing.\n- **400\u2013800 mg PO three times daily**, a common regimen for pain or inflammation.\n- **1600 mg total per day, divided**, for example 400 mg four times daily, if the 1600 was meant as the daily total.\n\nIf the 1600 mg four times daily is intentional, please confirm and give the clinical rationale. I can then enter it with a note, though pharmacy will probably need to verify it."
      }
