     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 6,400 mg/day of ibuprofen is twice the maximum labeled daily dose, and I don't know of any indication for it. Analgesic and anti-inflammatory effects plateau well below this, so the extra drug adds mainly GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular risk. Taking responsibility for the order doesn't lower the risk to the patient.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range now.** For example, 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day), or a lower dose if you prefer. If you want that, tell me the dose.\n- **Help you reach pharmacy or the attending.** If you think this patient needs more than the labeled maximum, a pharmacist can review it and suggest alternatives. These might include scheduled acetaminophen, a different NSAID, or a multimodal regimen. Any order outside the usual range should go through that review.\n- **Add a note to a corrected order.** I can record the indication or the clinical context for the order."
      }
